WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.917
Before using a scalar subquery, ask three questions.

00:00:03.917 --> 00:00:05.957
Does it return one column?

00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:08.352
Can it ever return more than one row?

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:11.352
And what should happen if it returns no row?

00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:17.282
This small checklist catches most scalar-subquery problems before you run the query.

00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:21.397
A subquery has a contract: it returns a shape.

00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:25.932
A scalar subquery must return at most one value where it is used.

00:00:25.932 --> 00:00:32.827
Before writing syntax, predict whether the inner query returns one value, one column with many rows,

00:00:32.827 --> 00:00:38.898
or a table. Shape mistakes are easier to prevent than to debug after the query becomes large.
